{
  "page": 3,
  "lines": [
    {
      "text": "Particle Markov Chain Monte Carlo Methods",
      "bbox": [
        232.71949768066406,
        39.52751922607422,
        407.94091796875,
        47.82143783569336
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "271",
      "bbox": [
        428.84783935546875,
        39.52751922607422,
        443.8038024902344,
        47.82143783569336
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "subsequently brieﬂy discussed and we then move on to describe standard MCMC strategies for",
      "bbox": [
        48.089698791503906,
        56.66524124145508,
        443.6058349609375,
        65.90057373046875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "inference in SSMs. Again we brieﬂy discuss their strengths and weaknesses and then show how",
      "bbox": [
        48.089698791503906,
        68.62037658691406,
        443.6129455566406,
        77.855712890625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "our novel methodology can address the same inference problems, albeit in a potentially more",
      "bbox": [
        48.089698791503906,
        80.57551574707031,
        443.60888671875,
        89.81085205078125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "efﬁcient way. No justiﬁcation for the validity of the algorithms presented is provided here—this",
      "bbox": [
        48.089698791503906,
        92.53065490722656,
        443.6008605957031,
        101.7659912109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "is postponed to Section 4.",
      "bbox": [
        48.089698791503906,
        104.48579406738281,
        156.8414306640625,
        113.72113037109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "2.1.",
      "bbox": [
        48.089698791503906,
        134.3536834716797,
        64.70732116699219,
        143.569091796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "State space models",
      "bbox": [
        74.0721664428711,
        134.3536834716797,
        161.56370544433594,
        143.569091796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Further on, we use the standard convention whereby capital letters denote random variables,",
      "bbox": [
        48.089698791503906,
        146.42835998535156,
        443.6087646484375,
        155.6636962890625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "whereas lower case letters are used for their values. Consider the following SSM, which is also",
      "bbox": [
        48.089698791503906,
        158.3834991455078,
        443.6098327636719,
        167.61883544921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "knownasahiddenMarkovmodel.Inthiscontext,ahiddenMarkovstateprocess{Xn;n⩾1}⊂X N",
      "bbox": [
        48.089698791503906,
        167.4798126220703,
        444.2561950683594,
        179.57452392578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "is characterized by its initial density X1∼μθ.·/ and transition probability density",
      "bbox": [
        48.089698791503906,
        181.45741271972656,
        385.3406982421875,
        192.67420959472656
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Xn+1|.Xn =x/∼fθ.·|x/,",
      "bbox": [
        196.0951385498047,
        199.8023223876953,
        294.10693359375,
        211.25921630859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": ".1/",
      "bbox": [
        431.1823425292969,
        200.63917541503906,
        443.605712890625,
        209.87451171875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "for some static parameter θ∈Θ which may be multidimensional. The process {Xn} is observed,",
      "bbox": [
        48.090484619140625,
        218.14710998535156,
        443.6109619140625,
        228.21963500976562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "not directly, but through another process {Yn;n⩾1}⊂YN. The observations are assumed to be",
      "bbox": [
        48.09075927734375,
        228.0799102783203,
        443.6106262207031,
        240.17459106445312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "conditionally independent given {Xn}, and their common marginal probability density is of the",
      "bbox": [
        48.09037780761719,
        242.05751037597656,
        443.60736083984375,
        252.12969970703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "form gθ.y|x/; i.e., for 1⩽n⩽m,",
      "bbox": [
        48.09027099609375,
        254.0126190185547,
        179.65673828125,
        265.08880615234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Yn|.X1, . . . ,Xn =x, . . . ,Xm/∼gθ.·|x/:",
      "bbox": [
        168.76364135742188,
        271.56048583984375,
        322.9324951171875,
        283.0174255371094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": ".2/",
      "bbox": [
        431.14227294921875,
        272.3973693847656,
        443.6054992675781,
        281.6326904296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Hereafter for any generic sequence {zn} we shall use zi:j to denote .zi,zi+1,. . . ,zj/.",
      "bbox": [
        48.09027099609375,
        289.9053039550781,
        396.1037292480469,
        301.4718933105469
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Our aim is to perform Bayesian inference in this context, conditional on some observations",
      "bbox": [
        58.053802490234375,
        302.6972961425781,
        443.6124572753906,
        311.9326171875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "y1:T for some T⩾1. When θ∈Θ is a known parameter, Bayesian inference relies on the posterior",
      "bbox": [
        48.09120178222656,
        313.8157043457031,
        443.6053161621094,
        325.5368957519531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "density pθ.x1:T |y1:T /∝pθ.x1:T , y1:T / where",
      "bbox": [
        48.09013366699219,
        325.7709045410156,
        227.28677368164062,
        337.4920959472656
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "pθ.x1:T , y1:T /=μθ.x1/",
      "bbox": [
        137.8236083984375,
        350.70440673828125,
        230.39454650878906,
        362.4255065917969
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "T\u0002",
      "bbox": [
        234.0532989501953,
        343.2323913574219,
        243.45799255371094,
        353.19500732421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "n=2",
      "bbox": [
        231.83360290527344,
        362.0836181640625,
        245.6517791748047,
        369.7384948730469
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "fθ.xn|xn−1/",
      "bbox": [
        247.12109375,
        350.7044982910156,
        295.91925048828125,
        361.9211730957031
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "T\u0002",
      "bbox": [
        299.5628967285156,
        343.23248291015625,
        308.96759033203125,
        353.1950988769531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "n=1",
      "bbox": [
        297.3583068847656,
        362.0837097167969,
        311.1764831542969,
        369.73858642578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "gθ.yn|xn/:",
      "bbox": [
        312.6155090332031,
        350.7044982910156,
        353.8735656738281,
        361.78070068359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": ".3/",
      "bbox": [
        431.1823425292969,
        351.5413818359375,
        443.605712890625,
        360.7767028808594
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "If θ is unknown, we ascribe a prior density p.θ/ to θ and Bayesian inference relies on the joint",
      "bbox": [
        48.090484619140625,
        375.8889465332031,
        443.60870361328125,
        385.9611511230469
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "density",
      "bbox": [
        48.08949279785156,
        388.6809387207031,
        78.2861328125,
        397.916259765625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "p.θ, x1:T |y1:T /∝pθ.x1:T ,y1:T /p.θ/:",
      "bbox": [
        173.20281982421875,
        403.2001037597656,
        318.49298095703125,
        414.9212951660156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": ".4/",
      "bbox": [
        431.13214111328125,
        404.0369873046875,
        443.60528564453125,
        413.2723083496094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "For non-linear non-Gaussian models, pθ.x1:T |y1:T / and p.θ,x1:T |y1:T / do not usually admit",
      "bbox": [
        48.090057373046875,
        422.5412902832031,
        443.6107482910156,
        434.1529235839844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "closed form expressions, making inference difﬁcult in practice. It is therefore necessary to resort",
      "bbox": [
        48.091583251953125,
        435.3332824707031,
        443.6056823730469,
        444.568603515625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "to approximations. Monte Carlo methods have been shown to provide a ﬂexible framework to",
      "bbox": [
        48.091583251953125,
        447.2884216308594,
        443.6119384765625,
        456.52374267578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "carry out inference in such models. It is impossible to provide a thorough review of the area",
      "bbox": [
        48.091583251953125,
        459.2435607910156,
        443.6126403808594,
        468.4788818359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "here and instead we brieﬂy review the underlying principles of MCMC and SMC methods for",
      "bbox": [
        48.091583251953125,
        471.19866943359375,
        443.60479736328125,
        480.4339904785156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "SSM models at a level that is sufﬁcient to understand our novel methodology.",
      "bbox": [
        48.091583251953125,
        483.1537780761719,
        373.66937255859375,
        492.38909912109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "2.2.",
      "bbox": [
        48.091583251953125,
        513.0216674804688,
        64.7092056274414,
        522.237060546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Sequential Monte Carlo algorithm for state space models",
      "bbox": [
        74.07405090332031,
        513.0216674804688,
        324.7530517578125,
        522.237060546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In the SSM context, SMC methods are a class of algorithms to approximate sequentially the",
      "bbox": [
        48.091583251953125,
        525.0963134765625,
        443.6066589355469,
        534.3316650390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "sequence of posterior densities {pθ.x1:n|y1:n/;n⩾1} as well as the sequence of marginal likeli-",
      "bbox": [
        48.091583251953125,
        536.214599609375,
        443.6114196777344,
        547.4317016601562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "hoods {pθ.y1:n/;n⩾1} for a given θ ∈Θ. More precisely such methods aim to approximate ﬁrst",
      "bbox": [
        48.09040832519531,
        548.1701049804688,
        443.6045227050781,
        559.3869018554688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "pθ.x1|y1/ and pθ.y1/, then pθ.x1:2|y1:2/ and pθ.y1:2/ and so on. In the context of SMC methods,",
      "bbox": [
        48.08930969238281,
        560.1253662109375,
        443.61029052734375,
        571.3421020507812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the posterior distributions that are associated with such densities are approximated by a set of",
      "bbox": [
        48.09100341796875,
        572.9173583984375,
        443.6041259765625,
        582.1527099609375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "N weighted random samples called particles, leading for any n⩾1 to the approximation",
      "bbox": [
        48.09100341796875,
        584.03564453125,
        417.44342041015625,
        594.1078491210938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ˆpθ.dx1:n|y1:n/:=",
      "bbox": [
        170.54429626464844,
        608.9691162109375,
        239.47634887695312,
        620.8943481445312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "N\u0003",
      "bbox": [
        242.31419372558594,
        601.4970703125,
        252.83470153808594,
        611.4596557617188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "k=1",
      "bbox": [
        240.860107421875,
        620.3483276367188,
        254.28456115722656,
        628.003173828125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Wk",
      "bbox": [
        255.72349548339844,
        607.6607666015625,
        268.8109130859375,
        616.939208984375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "nδXk",
      "bbox": [
        264.30126953125,
        608.9691162109375,
        282.4996337890625,
        620.2077026367188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "1:n.dx1:n/,",
      "bbox": [
        279.7110595703125,
        609.8059692382812,
        319.6588134765625,
        624.3499755859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
